</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Improving vessel segmentation with an auxiliary training target</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The multi-task Y-Net improves the overall Dice score of vessel segmentation on T1w data from <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.446" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.446</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.446</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.506" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.506</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.506</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(p = <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.09" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.09</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.09</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>, and Jaccard Score from <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.294" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.294</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.294</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.343" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.343</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.343</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(p = <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.09" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.09</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.09</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> when compared to a U-Net segmenting based on the same image data in experiment 1 (Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Improving Vessel Segmentation with Multi-Task Learning and Auxiliary Data Available Only During Model Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). Multi-task learning decreases mean surface distance from <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.615" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.615</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.615</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.929" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.929</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.929</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(p = <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.26" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.26</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.26</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> and results in gains in recall and slight decrease in precision for vessel segmentation compared to a single-task U-Net. <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Frangi filter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> in combination with Otsu thresholding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite> resulted in a Dice score of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.020" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.020</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.020</annotation></semantics></math>, Jaccard score of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.010" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.010</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.010</annotation></semantics></math> and a mean surface distance of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="75.822" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">75.822</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">75.822</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span><span id="S3.SS4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Improving</span> vessel segmentation with non-annotated imaging data</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In experiment 2 we trained a Y-Net-mix model with additional examples without annotations (Fig. <a href="#S2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 2.2 Model training and inference ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Improving Vessel Segmentation with Multi-Task Learning and Auxiliary Data Available Only During Model Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>b). Adding <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{I},\mathbf{J}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐉</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{I},\mathbf{J}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> pairs further improved segmentation accuracy compared with the Y-Net trained only on annotated cases (Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Improving Vessel Segmentation with Multi-Task Learning and Auxiliary Data Available Only During Model Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). With 30 additional examples the Dice score increased from <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.506" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.506</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.506</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.539" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.539</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.539</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(p ¡ 0.01)</span>, the Jaccard score from <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.343" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.343</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.343</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.376" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.376</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.376</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(p ¡ 0.01)</span> and the mean surface distance decreased from <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.929" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.929</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.929</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.621" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.621</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.621</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(p = 0.15)</span>. Recall of Y-Net-mix is better than U-Net and Y-Net, precision is better for the U-Net. Further analysis in section <a href="#S3.SS7" title="3.7 Segmentation accuracy for different vessel diameters ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Improving Vessel Segmentation with Multi-Task Learning and Auxiliary Data Available Only During Model Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a> revealed that this increase was due to small diameter vessels.
The multi-task loss function and automated search for optimal <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is not stable when the number of training samples for each task is substantially different. Therefore, we fixed <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> to values learned in the first experiment.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S3.F4.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03975v1/Fig5_a.svg" id="S3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/356;" width="476" height="356"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S3.F4.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03975v1/Fig5_b.svg" id="S3.F4.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/356;" width="476" height="356"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Segmentation accuracy (a) in relation to number of segmentations used for training for the whole vessel tree and (b) different vessel sizes between baseline and proposed methodologies. Multi-task learning with additional T1w/T1wce pairs benefits more if less annotations are used for training.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Combining transfer learning and multi-task learning</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The third experiment evaluated an alternative approach of combining data with and without annotations. Here, the Y-Net-TL was pretrained with <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{I},\mathbf{J}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐉</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{I},\mathbf{J}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> pairs (Fig. <a href="#S2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 2.2 Model training and inference ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Improving Vessel Segmentation with Multi-Task Learning and Auxiliary Data Available Only During Model Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>c) for <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> epochs. Then it was fine tuned (Fig. <a href="#S2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 2.2 Model training and inference ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Improving Vessel Segmentation with Multi-Task Learning and Auxiliary Data Available Only During Model Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>d) with <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{I},\mathbf{J},\mathbf{L}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐋</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{I},\mathbf{J},\mathbf{L}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> triplets for <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math> epochs in a <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-fold cross validation (<math id="S3.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> training samples, <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> test samples). Pretraining the Y-Net-TL with <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math> T1w/T1wce pairs improved the Dice score from <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.506" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.506</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.506</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.535" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.535</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.535</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(p ¡ 0.01)</span>, decreased the mean surface distance from <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.929" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.929</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.929</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.476" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.476</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.476</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(p = 0.06)</span>, and improved recall over the Y-Net (Table <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 3.2 Experiment set-up ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Improving Vessel Segmentation with Multi-Task Learning and Auxiliary Data Available Only During Model Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). The successive addition of T1w/T1wce training pairs for pretraining resulted in increasingly better segmentation accuracy (Dice). Overall accuracy is comparable to the strategy evaluated in section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Improving vessel segmentation with non-annotated imaging data ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Improving Vessel Segmentation with Multi-Task Learning and Auxiliary Data Available Only During Model Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Dice, mean surface distance, recall and precision related to the vessel thickness between baseline U-Net, proposed Y-Net, Y-Net-mix trained with additional 30 T1w/T1wce training pairs without annotation and Y-Net-TL (Y-Net is pretrained with 30 T1w/T1wce pairs without annotations and fine tuned with T1w, T1wce and segmentation). Percentage values relate to affiliation of total vessel volume.</figcaption>
